# fixedbugs, defect 2317, 2026-11-07: two cases of one name with two payloads.
# Before, the construction and the arm reached the second, so `.one(x: 1)` was
# told that `Turn.one` has nothing called `x`, a type mismatch beside it, and
# the `match` that it did not cover `.one`, three false messages and none
# naming the mistake. Now the second case is refused, naming the first, and
# the first is what the construction and the arm read.
variant Turn
    one
        x: i64
    one  #~ case_declared_twice
        y: str

function main()
    t: Turn = .one(x: 1)

    match t
        .one p => print(p.x)
